[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69708,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diverticular carcinoma is a carcinoma that is located in a diverticulum in the urinary tract.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69709,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "<p>8120/3 Invasive urothelial carcinoma (code to site)</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-12T09:17:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69710,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GC01.2 &amp; XH74S1 Diverticulum of bladder &amp; Adenocarcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>GC01.2 &amp; XH8EH1 Diverticulum of bladder &amp; Transitional cell carcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>GC01.2 &amp; XH0945 Diverticulum of bladder &amp; Squamous cell carcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69711,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> intradiverticular carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69712,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69713,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most types and subtypes of carcinomas of the urinary tract can occur in diverticula {24934450}. Common locations are the lateral urinary bladder walls close to the ureteric orifices and the dome {24934450; 23375647; 23540860}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69714,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clinical features are similar to those of non-diverticular carcinomas in the urinary tract. Cystoscopy, urine cytology, ultrasonography, and cross-sectional imaging studies often establish the diagnosis. A narrow or concealed diverticular orifice might limit the sensitivity of cystoscopy {24934450}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69715,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diverticular carcinomas are rare, estimated to account for &lt;&nbsp;1% (range: 0.8&ndash;10.8%) of urinary bladder tumours {24934450; 3118548; 9372877; 3095564; 6405057}. Most patients present in the sixth decade of life and most cases occur in men {24934450}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69716,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Risk factors for diverticular carcinomas are similar to those of other carcinomas in the urinary tract. The presence of a urinary bladder diverticulum indicates a higher risk of subsequent bladder cancer development {19415955; 22877502; 31613877; 24934450}. When diverticular and bladder tumours are present simultaneously, tumours are more commonly found within the diverticulum {23375647; 9372877}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69717,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Urinary bladder cancer risk may be increased through urinary stasis in diverticula, prolonging the effect of carcinogens and potentially leading to increased inflammation, recurrent infections, calculi, and metaplastic and dysplastic changes {19076130; 25863833; 24934450; 25457532; 23540860; 23375647; 19415955}. No specific molecular pathology has been described.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69718,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diverticular carcinomas can be single or multiple. Tumour size varies, and they can weigh as much as 14&nbsp;kg {24934450; 28246375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69719,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histopathology of diverticular carcinomas resembles that of other carcinomas in the urinary tract. The most common type is urothelial carcinoma. Other tumour types seem to be more frequent in diverticula than in the main urinary bladder {19415955; 6430029; 25425482; 23375647; 23540860}. Diverticula do not have a detrusor muscle layer, but they often have a hypertrophic layer of muscularis mucosae {25425482}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69720,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Urine cytology is useful in diagnosis and follow-up, mostly in high-grade disease. A narrow diverticular orifice might limit cytological test sensitivity {24934450}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69721,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69722,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a carcinoma arising from or mainly located in a diverticulum; morphological criteria of non-diverticular carcinomas of the urinary tract also apply for diverticular carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69723,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The TNM system is used for diverticular carcinomas. However, as diverticula lack detrusor muscle, pT2 stage cannot be assigned. Upstaging from a transurethral resection specimen to radical cystectomy is common {23375647}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69724,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognostic significance of tumour stages for diverticular carcinomas compared with those for cancers of the main bladder are under debate {14532771; 22732640}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:05:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]